  "notes": [
    "Follows the -DUCIR verb pattern (same as *conducir*, *producir*, *traducir*)",
    "Irregular yo present: *abduzco* (c→zc before a/o)",
    "Irregular preterite stem: *abduj-* (abduje, abdujiste, abdujo, abdujimos, abdujeron)",
    "Subjuntivo from yo stem: *abduzc-* (abduzca, abduzcas…)",
    "Past participle: *abducido*",
    "Most commonly used in sci-fi/UFO contexts: *Los extraterrestres abducen a los humanos* — Aliens abduct humans",
    "Also used in medical/anatomical contexts: to abduct a limb (move it away from the body's midline)",
    "Related: *la abducción* = abduction; *el/la abducido/a* = abductee; *secuestrar* = to kidnap (more common for human kidnapping)"
  ],
